 "notes": "ratopati.com is a Laravel site with no usable sitemap (every unknown path, including /sitemap.xml and /wp-sitemap.xml, is answered with the SPA home page), no JSON API (app.min.js only calls /api/v1/translate), an RSS feed (/feed) capped at 30 items that ignores ?page=, and a /latest-news list that also ignores ?page=. What does work: /category/<slug>?page=N paginates server-side (~94 story links per page, newest first), and every /story/<id> page carries JSON-LD datePublished. Story ids are autoincrement in publish order (~250 ids per day), so the script probes one /story/<id> every 200 ids to build date anchors (40 anchors, 2026-09-21..2026-10-27) and dates every listing id by linear interpolation between its bracketing anchors. /story/<id> without the slug resolves fine, so slugs are taken from the listings. Result: 1105 URLs across 31 days, 81 requests, 62s. 5/5 sampled articles re-fetched with a page date within 1 day and 1500+ chars of text (min 2151 chars).",
